/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (Financial institutions face losses when borrowers fail to repay loans. Early identification of potential defaulters can improve lending decisions and reduce financial risk. This project focuses on predicting loan default using machine learning techniques. Different models such as Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest, and XGBoost were used to analyze borrower and loan-related information. Data preprocessing, feature engineering, and model evaluation were performed to identify the best prediction model. The goal of this project is to help improve loan risk assessment and decision-making.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
